I'll pass this turn, too.

251
00:14:02,160 --> 00:14:06,440
But next time, when my Ghoul's
free to attack, I'll wipe you out!

252
00:14:08,540 --> 00:14:09,600
So, Solomon,

253
00:14:09,900 --> 00:14:15,120
on my next turn I'll be free to attack,
But I'm going to pass this turn.

254
00:14:15,340 --> 00:14:17,720
If that's really what you want to do.

255
00:14:18,020 --> 00:14:20,314
What card are you waiting for, Solomon?

256
00:14:20,600 --> 00:14:21,920
That's my secret.

257
00:14:27,320 --> 00:14:28,732
What's the matter, Yugi?

258
00:14:28,860 --> 00:14:30,801
Didn't you get the card you need?

259
00:14:34,180 --> 00:14:36,760
So, Solomon, did you
get the card you need?

260
00:14:42,600 --> 00:14:44,718
Come now, don't keep me in suspense.

261
00:14:47,000 --> 00:14:48,980
I surrender, Arthur.

262
00:14:49,220 --> 00:14:50,240
You win.

263
00:14:57,140 --> 00:14:58,980
I surrender, Rebecca.

264
00:15:00,420 --> 00:15:02,060
I can't believe it!

265
00:15:02,420 --> 00:15:03,361
Yugi's given up!

266
00:15:10,140 --> 00:15:11,860
The game's over, Rebecca.

267
00:15:13,680 --> 00:15:14,510
Unbelievable.

268
00:15:17,060 --> 00:15:18,060
Yugi, why?

269
00:15:18,360 --> 00:15:20,066
You can't just give up, Yugi.

270
00:15:23,540 --> 00:15:24,960
You mean I win?

271
00:15:25,200 --> 00:15:26,740
Yes, you win, Rebecca.

272
00:15:27,680 --> 00:15:28,510
Bravo!

273
00:15:28,593 --> 00:15:29,423
Yay, me!

274
00:15:29,506 --> 00:15:30,398
We beat him, Teddy!

275
00:15:30,560 --> 00:15:32,540
Rebecca the Genius wins!

276
00:15:33,740 --> 00:15:34,860
I don't get it.

277
00:15:34,960 --> 00:15:36,157
Why did you surrender?

278
00:15:36,240 --> 00:15:38,057
Yeah, what's up with that, Youg?

279
00:15:38,140 --> 00:15:38,970
I won!

280
00:15:39,060 --> 00:15:40,589
Now give me the blue eyes!

281
00:15:46,100 --> 00:15:47,720
You tore it! Oh no!

282
00:15:47,920 --> 00:15:50,337
You destroyed my
grandfather's favorite card!

283
00:15:50,420 --> 00:15:51,337
It wasn't me, Rebecca.

284
00:15:51,420 --> 00:15:54,077
First you steal it, then
you lie, then you ruin it!

285
00:15:54,160 --> 00:15:55,980
You despicable, mean man!

286
00:15:56,160 --> 00:15:57,984
I treasured that card, Rebecca.

287
00:15:58,140 --> 00:15:59,937
I would never have destroyed it.

288
00:16:00,020 --> 00:16:02,157
I've heard just about enough of your lies!

289
00:16:02,240 --> 00:16:03,920
Rebecca, behave yourself.

290
00:16:05,800 --> 00:16:07,380
Grandpa? Arthur?

291
00:16:07,600 --> 00:16:09,071
Arthur, is it really you?

292
00:16:09,980 --> 00:16:11,880
It's been a long time, Solomon.

293
00:16:12,200 --> 00:16:14,660
Far too long, my dear old friend.

294
00:16:14,820 --> 00:16:18,797
I do hope my precocious granddaughter
hasn't caused you too much trouble.

295
00:16:18,880 --> 00:16:20,060
Can you forgive her?

296
00:16:20,620 --> 00:16:21,540
For what?

297
00:16:21,920 --> 00:16:26,080
Rebecca, did you know Yugi was
actually the winner of your duel? No!

298
00:16:26,280 --> 00:16:27,380
Grandpa, I won!

299
00:16:28,220 --> 00:16:30,217
Yugi, you're just like your grandfather.

300
00:16:30,300 --> 00:16:33,520
You're a generous young man
and a very fine duelist.

301
00:16:36,320 --> 00:16:37,440
I knew it.

302
00:16:37,920 --> 00:16:40,660
Rebecca, have a look at this card. Huh?

303
00:16:41,240 --> 00:16:43,160
It's a card called Soul Release.

304
00:16:43,600 --> 00:16:46,157
If Yugi had played this
card in the final turn,

305
00:16:46,240 --> 00:16:48,337
you would have been defeated for certain.

306
00:16:48,420 --> 00:16:52,857
With Soul Release, Yugi could have freed
up to five cards from his graveyard.

307
00:16:52,940 --> 00:16:53,770
Or yours.

308
00:16:54,040 --> 00:16:55,757
Do you realize what that means?

309
00:16:55,840 --> 00:17:00,800
Your Shadow Ghoul's attack power would
have instantly dropped from 2800 to 2300.

310
00:17:01,240 --> 00:17:05,800
Yugi's Dark Magician had an attack
power of 2500, and therefore...

311
00:17:07,420 --> 00:17:10,560
Uh, you mean Yugi really
never had to surrender?

312
00:17:10,900 --> 00:17:11,740
Then why?

313
00:17:12,780 --> 00:17:14,015
Don't you understand?

314
00:17:14,300 --> 00:17:16,337
Yugi wanted to show you that there's much

315
00:17:16,420 --> 00:17:18,677
more to dueling than
just winning and losing.

316
00:17:18,760 --> 00:17:20,597
He wanted you to see that the way to the

317
00:17:20,680 --> 00:17:23,327
heart of the cards is
through your own heart.

318
00:17:24,420 --> 00:17:27,697
After that tomb collapsed and
we'd bet our last drop of water

319
00:17:27,780 --> 00:17:32,000
on the duel Solomon also sacrificed
a victory to save my life

320
00:17:33,900 --> 00:17:36,800
I felt weak, overcome by the heat

321
00:17:38,520 --> 00:17:40,080
Hold on, my friend

322
00:17:41,980 --> 00:17:45,980
You didn't have to surrender I
couldn't let you lose this duel,

323
00:17:46,100 --> 00:17:49,360
Arthur You need the
water Solomon, thank you

324
00:17:56,580 --> 00:17:57,800
We did it!

325
00:17:57,980 --> 00:17:59,215
We've broken through!

326
00:17:59,460 --> 00:18:00,800
Are you down there?

327
00:18:01,400 --> 00:18:02,640
Did you survive?

328
00:18:04,240 --> 00:18:06,380
He saved my life, Rebecca.

329
00:18:06,900 --> 00:18:08,140
But there's more.

330
00:18:08,440 --> 00:18:10,060
In my duel with Solomon,

331
00:18:10,360 --> 00:18:13,077
it's true that I sent any
number of monsters to the

332
00:18:13,160 --> 00:18:16,572
graveyard to bring the Shadow
Ghoul to its ultimate power.

333
00:18:17,160 --> 00:18:21,200
But I never failed to honor those
monsters for their sacrifice.

334
00:18:22,280 --> 00:18:23,110
In their own way,

335
00:18:23,193 --> 00:18:27,296
they were every bit as important to
me as the Shadow Ghoul card itself.

336
00:18:28,400 --> 00:18:33,106
Even more than the monsters, though, a
duelist must always respect his opponent.

337
00:18:33,460 --> 00:18:34,540
In Solomon's case,

338
00:18:34,740 --> 00:18:39,540
I felt such respect and gratitude that
I gave him my Blue-Eyes White Dragon.

339
00:18:39,880 --> 00:18:43,409
Yeah, and he showed his respect
and thanks by ripping it up!

340
00:18:43,920 --> 00:18:46,440
It was damaged, Arthur. Forgive me.

341
00:18:46,840 --> 00:18:48,377
That doesn't matter, Solomon.

342
00:18:48,460 --> 00:18:51,597
What matters is that you kept
it as a token of our friendship.

343
00:18:51,680 --> 00:18:55,660
You valued the card not for its
rarity, but for what it represents,

344
00:18:55,900 --> 00:18:57,440
the bond between us.

345
00:18:57,840 --> 00:18:59,657
Now do you understand, Rebecca?

346
00:18:59,740 --> 00:19:02,797
Great duels can form the
basis of great and lasting

347
00:19:02,880 --> 00:19:06,760
friendships because the cards
are about heart. My heart?

348
00:19:06,960 --> 00:19:08,548
The heart of every duelist.

349
00:19:08,680 --> 00:19:10,217
And the heart of the cards.

350
00:19:10,300 --> 00:19:12,653
That's what Yugi was trying to show you.

351
00:19:13,660 --> 00:19:15,640
Oh, Yugi, I'm sorry.

352
00:19:16,020 --> 00:19:17,200
It's okay, Rebecca.

353
00:19:18,100 --> 00:19:20,400
You mean you forgive me? Sure.

354
00:19:20,740 --> 00:19:21,975
Here, take this card.

355
00:19:22,780 --> 00:19:24,140
The tie's a friendship.

356
00:19:24,740 --> 00:19:26,560
Yeah, I'd like you to have it.

357
00:19:26,720 --> 00:19:27,661
Thank you, Yugi.

358
00:19:28,800 --> 00:19:32,153
Say, Solomon, it's been ages
since you and I have dueled.

359
00:19:32,260 --> 00:19:35,320
Is that a challenge I
hear, Arthur? Oh, wow!

360
00:19:35,780 --> 00:19:37,397
This I gotta see, dueling grandpa's!

361
00:19:37,480 --> 00:19:38,310
Mr.

362
00:19:38,393 --> 00:19:40,057
Moto, remember, you just
got out of the hospital.

363
00:19:40,140 --> 00:19:44,846
Yes, but I could out-duel any of you young
Turks, even if I was still in a coma.
